{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>The camel's saddle.</b> A term of cushions and coverlets — as its Targum renders: בַּעֲבִיטָא דְגַמְלָא. It is a pack-saddle made in the shape of a cushion. And in Eruvin (16a) we learned: they surrounded it with עֲבִיטִין — and these are camel packs; בשט\"ו בְּלַעַ\"ז."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The la'az בשט\"ו likely corresponds to Old French baste or bast, a pack-saddle (Latin bastum)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:32.332569702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}